From fa3b76c171ddd5cbd438c51edd6485c72b22dc73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:05:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] amigaos: EH data is always absolute (DW_EH_PE_absptr)

m68k.h's ASM_PREFERRED_EH_DATA_FORMAT picks DW_EH_PE_pcrel, with
DW_EH_PE_indirect for global references, whenever flag_pic is set, and
-fbaserel, -fbaserel32, -resident and -resident32 set it. The indirect
references go through per-unit .data.rel.local.LDFCM* pools, and
.gcc_except_table reaches them with 32-bit PC-relative relocations from one
hunk to another, which the hunk format cannot express: every base-relative
C++ link printed "reloc for .data.rel.local.LDFCM0 is out of range" and the
type table held garbage, so catch by type could not match.

On AmigaOS the EH data is now always DW_EH_PE_absptr, which RELOC32
relocates in every code model, as it already was in the absolute one.
---
 gcc/config/m68k/amigaos.h | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/m68k/amigaos.h b/gcc/config/m68k/amigaos.h
index 183399f..caf5f6c 100644
--- a/gcc/config/m68k/amigaos.h
+++ b/gcc/config/m68k/amigaos.h
@@ -139,6 +139,15 @@ amiga_select_section (tree decl, int reloc ATTRIBUTE_UNUSED,
 #define ALIGN_ASM_OP "\t.align\t"
 #endif
 
+/* EH data (.eh_frame, .gcc_except_table) is always absolute on AmigaOS.
+   m68k.h picks DW_EH_PE_pcrel (and indirect for globals) when flag_pic, which
+   -fbaserel, -fbaserel32, -resident and -resident32 set; but a PC-relative
+   reference from the except table to a typeinfo pointer in a data hunk
+   crosses hunks, which the hunk format cannot express ("reloc ... out of
+   range"). RELOC32 relocates an absolute pointer in every code model.  */
+#undef ASM_PREFERRED_EH_DATA_FORMAT
+#define ASM_PREFERRED_EH_DATA_FORMAT(CODE, GLOBAL) DW_EH_PE_absptr
+
 /* GAS supports alignment up to 32768 bytes.  */
 #undef ASM_OUTPUT_ALIGN
 #define ASM_OUTPUT_ALIGN(FILE, LOG)					\
-- 
2.53.0

